VII. CONCLUSIONS
In this paper, we have discussed advancements in SATCOM systems, in particular, with a focus on requirements of 5G and 6G communication systems. We have discussed the enabling technologies and advancements in communication protocols, their benefits, limitations, and open problems with respect to multiplexing, modulations, channel encoding and SDR-based platforms for SATCOM systems. We have underscored that the rapidly growing demand for various services, and the conflicting requirement of higher throughput, lower latency and massive device connections require integration of space and terrestrial services at multi-layer level. Moreover, the rapid advancements in satellite constellations, inter-satellite and intra-satellite communication require integration of existing and next generation architecture to provide services and meet quality of service standards. We have highlighted the extensive research in adaptive modulation and coding schemes, URLLC channel encoding techniques for real time applications, LDPC and PC, modern multiplexing schemes such as OFDMA, and NOMA for enhancing spectral and power efficiency and the need for inter-satellite communication systems to meet the growing demand for network services and applications.
